{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"jovial-subcranial-conch","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n\nA LINK whose stored `target_id` is a short form (for example a 4-hex quad) that DOES resolve to exactly 1 ticket cannot be removed by `unlink`. `process_link` (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:200-214`) resolves the raw target at replay, so `show` lists the canonical id. `_get_link_info` (`src/rebar/_commands/unlink.py:42`) compares the stored raw string against the canonical id `unlink_core` resolved, so neither form matches.\n\nReproduced in a sandbox store on 2026-11-03: a `caused_by` LINK written with target `<quad>` (unique). `show` listed the full id. `rebar.unlink(bug, <quad>, \"caused_by\")` and `rebar.unlink(bug, <full id>, \"caused_by\")` both failed with \"Error: no LINK event found ... targeting '<full id>' with relation 'caused_by'\". The dep stayed.\n\n`_is_active_link` (`src/rebar/graph/_links.py:84`) compares stored raw targets the same way.\n\n## Impact\n\nLinks written with a non-canonical target before `rebar link` / close started refusing unresolved targets (surprising-fruticose-herring) cannot be removed through a supported command once their short target becomes unique, even though `show` displays them as ordinary links.\n\n## Not yet checked\n\nHow many stored LINK events in the live store carry a non-canonical `target_id`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar unlink <source> <target> [relation]` removes a net-active link whose stored `target_id` resolves to the same canonical id the input resolves to. A unit test writes a LINK with a unique 4-hex target and removes it by both the 4-hex and the full id.","id":"d81e-b1e1-1807-4a9c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"unlink cannot remove a link whose stored short target resolves to a ticket"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793701408574961001,"uuid":"01c67ca2-b838-41c0-8e1d-13168619aab1"}